  "problem": "Three bags, $A,B,$ and $C,$ contain marbles. Bag $A$ contains $12$ red and $8$ green marbles, while bag $B$ contains $14$ red and $6$ green marbles. A bag is selected at random, and a marble is randomly selected from the bag. If the probability that the selected marble is green is $\\frac{2}{5},$  what proportion of marbles from bag $C$ are green?",
